  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Arya the monkey is trapped inside an N×MN\\times MN×M grid!\n\nThe grid has NNN rows (numbered 111 to NNN from top to bottom) and MMM columns (numbered 111 to MMM from left to right). The cell at the intersection of row iii and column jjj is denoted (i,j)(i, j)(i,j).\n\nArya wants to escape the grid, of course - but first, he needs information.\n\nArya is initially at cell (X0,Y0)(X_0, Y_0)(X0​,Y0​) of the grid, and can move to other cells by jumping to them. Arya's jump strength is LLL, meaning Arya can jump **exactly** LLL units in any of the four directions up, down, left, and right.\n\nFormally, from cell (a,b)(a, b)(a,b), Arya can jump to the following cells: (a−L,b),(a+L,b),(a,b−L),(a,b+L)(a-L, b), (a+L, b), (a, b-L), (a, b+L)(a−L,b),(a+L,b),(a,b−L),(a,b+L) (provided the destination is within the grid).\n\nHow many **distinct** cells in the grid can Arya reach using zero or more jumps of this form?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case will contain five space-separated integers N,M,X0,Y0,N, M, X_0, Y_0,N,M,X0​,Y0​, and LLL — the dimensions of the grid, Arya's starting position, and Arya's jump strength.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing the answer: the number of **distinct** cells Arya can reach within the grid.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N,M,L≤1091 \\leq N,M,L \\leq 10^91≤N,M,L≤109",
      "1≤X0≤N1 \\leq X_0 \\leq N1≤X0​≤N",
      "1≤Y0≤M1 \\leq Y_0 \\leq M1≤Y0​≤M"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 1 1 1 1\n3 4 2 3 2\n12345 2345 543 345 65\n1000000000 1000000000 23 7654 1",
        "output": "1\n2\n6840\n1000000000000000000",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There's only one cell in the grid.\nTest case 222: The grid is of dimensions 3×43\\times 43×4, and Arya starts at (2,3)(2, 3)(2,3) with L=2L = 2L=2.\nArya can jump to (2,1)(2, 1)(2,1), and that's the only other cell that can be visited.\nTest case 444: Since L=1L = 1L=1, Arya can reach every cell in the grid.\nThere are 109×109=101810^9 \\times 10^9 = 10^{18}109×109=1018 cells in the grid - so this is the answer.\nNote that the answer may exceed the limit of a 32-bit integer."
      }
    ]
  },
